+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope; Correcting One Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined changing or cancelling a visit once booked. The [2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed the row deliberate. It also required any later narrowing to be a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+A request on 2026-09-11 observed that visits can only be created, never corrected. The owner decided on the row at intake. The intake records the decision but no rationale beyond that observation.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** A booked visit stays immutable, and a wrongly entered visit cannot be fixed.
+2. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen by the owner). Correcting a booked visit's date and description comes into scope; cancelling stays out.
+3. **Retire NG-5.** Both correction and cancellation come into scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+NG-5 now covers cancelling a visit once booked. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is `REQ-VIS-003`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A booked visit is no longer immutable. Its date and description can change, under the same rules as booking.
+- The 2026-08-08 ADR's NG-4 decision stands unchanged: deleting an owner, a pet, or a visit stays out of scope.
+- No page links to the correction yet. The owner's decision, quoted from the same intake: "The edit form is reachable by its URL alone: the owner detail page gains no edit link in this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request."
+- Because a correction follows booking's rules, a visit dated today or earlier cannot keep its date through a correction. The PRD's Open Questions records whether that reading is intended.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and preamble.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement.
+
+## References
+
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the NG-5 decision this ADR narrows.
